From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:43:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D215 server: creating a session with an unknown agent is a
 404

Upstream: POST /api/session records any agent ID it is given; a session created with an agent that does not
exist only fails when it first prompts ("Agent not found").
Fixed: like D206, an agent given on create is checked in the session's location (the parent's for a child) once
its plugins have loaded, and an unknown one answers 404 AgentNotFoundError ("Agent not found: <id>"); nothing is
created. The route declares the location errors this can return (404 LocationNotFoundError, 503 when plugins do not
finish loading). The agent check is shared with the switch route.
Scenarios: session-api-crud.test.ts "create a session with invalid payloads" (new request); session-api-control.test.ts
"a session on an unknown agent fails its turn" (creating it is now a 404, so the session comes from an import)
Upstream tests: packages/server/test/session-create.test.ts adds a test; client and openapi.json regenerated

